 "title": "Jeep J-Series Engines by Year (1972–1988)",
 "description": "Every factory engine in the Jeep J-series pickup by year, 1972–1988: AMC's 258 six and 304, 360 and 401 V8s in the J10 and J20 trucks.",
 "intro": [
  "The Jeep pickup sold as the Gladiator from 1963 was renamed the J-series for 1972 and built until 1988. The J10 was the half-ton; the heavier J20 always came with a V8. Jeep's truck literature stopped quoting horsepower after 1973, so most later years show no rating. The 1963–1971 trucks are on the Gladiator page.",
  "Pick a year to see every engine offered that model year, with its code, rated horsepower and the trims it came in. Each engine links to its full specs."
 ],
